why Every Horde quest of Blackfathom Deeps in one run, lead-in included.

# Blackfathom Deeps' Horde quests in one guide: Tsunaman's lead-in, Je'neu
# Sancrea at Zoram'gar, the shore by the door, one run, then the hand-ins.
# Steps already done are passed over, so the guide picks up wherever the chain
# stands.
#
# The quests: Tsunaman's 6562 Trouble in the Deeps (to Je'neu) -> 6563 The
# Essence of Aku'Mai (twenty sapphires on the shore by the door); Je'neu's 6921
# Amongst the Ruins (the Fathom Core inside); the Damp Note (item 16790, from
# a Blackfathom Tide Priestess) starts 6564 Allegiance to the Old Gods -> 6565
# (Lorgus Jett); Argent Guard Thaelrid's 6561 Blackfathom Villainy (taken
# inside; Kelris' head, for Bashana Runetotem); Baron Aquanis' Strange Water
# Globe (item 16782) starts 6922 Baron Aquanis.
#
# Left out: the Warlocks' 1740 The Orb of Soran'ruk (its large fragment comes
# from Shadowfang Keep); 78917 The Heart of the Void and 908 Amongst the
# Ruins, which have no giver in the data.
#
# Inside: nothing in the data places the bosses, Thaelrid or the Fathom Stone
# inside, so their goals stand at the door (@15.1,13.2, Ashenvale) with
# `group 5`. The bosses come in the order of the client's dungeon journal
# (Ghamoo-ra, Lady Sarevess, Geilhast, Lorgus Jett, Old Serra'kis, Twilight
# Lord Kelris, Aku'mai; Baron Aquanis optional), not of a recorded run. Every
# quest goal is counted by the quest log, so a group that takes them in
# another order still gets each step ticked. The sapphires and the Tide
# Priestess stand outside the dungeon, on the shore around the door.
#
# Sources (facts only):
# - Quests, NPCs, items, objects and rewards: Polestar's reference data
#   (data/forever, built from QuestieDB Forever 1.1.4) and Polestar 0.4.1.1's
#   Codex page for the dungeon.
# - The door: players' recordings, as Polestar's Codex holds them
#   (data/codex/entrances.json).
# - The dungeon's size, levels and bosses: the client's group finder and
#   dungeon journal, as Polestar's Codex page holds them (five players, levels
#   24 to 32).
# INGAME: where inside do Argent Guard Thaelrid and the Fathom Stone stand?

step Tsunaman
  accept 6562

step Je'neu Sancrea
  zone Ashenvale
  tip At Zoram'gar.
  turnin 6562
  accept 6563
  accept 6921

step The shore by the door
  tip Outside the dungeon: the Sapphires of Aku'Mai lie around the door, and a Blackfathom Tide Priestess here may drop a Damp Note, which starts a quest.
  collect 16784 x20 quest 6563.1
  collect 16790 optional -- The Damp Note, if it drops.

step The Damp Note
  when has 16790
  accept 6564

step Je'neu Sancrea
  turnin 6563

step Je'neu Sancrea
  when onquest 6564
  turnin 6564
  accept 6565

step To Blackfathom Deeps
  tip A dungeon for five players of level 24 to 32.
  enter "Blackfathom Deeps" @15.1,13.2

step Argent Guard Thaelrid
  tip He waits inside, with a quest for the Horde too.
  accept 6561 @15.1,13.2

step The Fathom Stone
  collect 16762 quest 6921.1 @15.1,13.2 group 5

step Lorgus Jett
  when onquest 6565
  tip The fourth boss in the client's journal, after Ghamoo-ra, Lady Sarevess and Geilhast.
  kill 12902 quest 6565.1 @15.1,13.2 group 5

step Twilight Lord Kelris
  tip The sixth boss in the client's journal, after Old Serra'kis; Aku'mai comes last. Kelris' head is for Bashana Runetotem. Baron Aquanis, a boss off the journal's line, may drop a Strange Water Globe, which starts a quest.
  collect 5881 quest 6561.1 @15.1,13.2 group 5
  collect 16782 @15.1,13.2 optional -- The Strange Water Globe, if you meet Baron Aquanis.

step Baron Aquanis
  when has 16782
  accept 6922

step Je'neu Sancrea
  turnin 6921

step Je'neu Sancrea
  when onquest 6565
  turnin 6565

step Je'neu Sancrea
  when onquest 6922
  turnin 6922

step Bashana Runetotem
  zone Thunder Bluff
  turnin 6561
